% Two estates are divided among descendants and a surviving spouse without a
% will, after the French Code civil. Children inherit equally (Article 735).
% A child who died first, renounced or is unworthy is represented by their
% own descendants, to any depth, and each branch shares what its head would
% have had (Articles 751 to 755). A spouse chooses the usufruct of the whole
% estate or a quarter of it, but takes the quarter when a child is not the
% spouse's (Article 757).
% Marie's estate of 240000 goes in four shares to a daughter, two
% grandchildren through a son who died first, and a granddaughter through an
% unworthy daughter; her husband keeps the usufruct. Jan's estate of 90000
% gives his wife a quarter, although she chose the usufruct, because his son
% Tom is not hers; Tom's share goes on to a grandchild and a great-grandchild.
% Shows recursion through generations, division by a count of branches,
% negation of derived relations, nested negation and sums that check that
% every estate is divided in full.
% A simplified model of descendants and a spouse only: it leaves out wills,
% the reserved portion, other relatives and earlier gifts.
% Source https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/texte_lc/LEGITEXT000006070721 (Articles 726, 735, 751 to 755, 757 and 805)

the templates are:
    *a person* died leaving an estate of *an amount*,
    *a person* is a child of *a parent*,
    *a person* died before *a deceased*,
    *a person* was convicted of killing *a deceased*,
    *a person* renounced the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* is the spouse of *a deceased*,
    *a person* chose the usufruct,
    *a person* is unworthy to inherit from *a deceased*,
    *a person* does not inherit in person from *a deceased*,
    *a person* is an heir in person of *a deceased*,
    *a person* leads to an heir of *a deceased*,
    *a person* is cut off from the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* is a branch of *a parent* in the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* has the usufruct of the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* takes a quarter of the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* receives *an amount* from *a deceased* as surviving spouse,
    the descendants of *a deceased* share *an amount*,
    *a person* passes on *an amount* in the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* is represented in the estate of *a deceased*,
    *a person* inherits *an amount* from *a deceased*,
    the shares of the estate of *a deceased* add up to *an amount*.

the knowledge base succession includes:

% Article 726: whoever is convicted of intentionally killing the deceased is
% unworthy to inherit.
a person is unworthy to inherit from a deceased
    if the person was convicted of killing the deceased.

% An heir in person survived the deceased, is not unworthy and did not
% renounce; a renouncer is deemed never to have been an heir (Article 805).
a person does not inherit in person from a deceased
    if the person died before the deceased.

a person does not inherit in person from a deceased
    if the person is unworthy to inherit from the deceased.

a person does not inherit in person from a deceased
    if the person renounced the estate of the deceased.

% A child of the deceased, or of someone in the line who does not inherit in
% person, can take in person. Only the line of the deceased is followed, not
% the other parent, so a child of both spouses is counted once; the totals
% below would show a share counted twice.
a person is an heir in person of a deceased
    if the deceased died leaving an estate of an amount
    and the person is a child of the deceased
    and it is not the case that
        the person does not inherit in person from the deceased.

a person is an heir in person of a deceased
    if the person is a child of an other person
    and the other person does not inherit in person from a deceased
    and it is not the case that
        the person does not inherit in person from the deceased.

% Article 752: representation goes down the line without limit.
a person leads to an heir of a deceased
    if the person is an heir in person of the deceased.

a person leads to an heir of a deceased
    if an other person is a child of the person
    and the other person leads to an heir of the deceased.

% A child with no heir in person anywhere below them takes no share, and the
% others share it instead.
a person is cut off from the estate of a deceased
    if the deceased died leaving an estate of an amount
    and the person is a child of a parent
    and it is not the case that
        the person leads to an heir of the deceased.

a person is a branch of a parent in the estate of a deceased
    if the person is a child of the parent
    and the deceased died leaving an estate of an amount
    and it is not the case that
        the person is cut off from the estate of the deceased.

% Article 757: the spouse chooses the usufruct of the whole estate only when
% every branch descends from both spouses.
a person has the usufruct of the estate of a deceased
    if the person is the spouse of the deceased
    and it is not the case that
        the person died before the deceased
    and the person chose the usufruct
    and it is not the case that
        an other person is a branch of the deceased in the estate of the deceased
        and it is not the case that
            the other person is a child of the person.

a person takes a quarter of the estate of a deceased
    if the person is the spouse of the deceased
    and it is not the case that
        the person died before the deceased
    and it is not the case that
        the person has the usufruct of the estate of the deceased.

a person receives an amount from a deceased as surviving spouse
    if the person takes a quarter of the estate of the deceased
    and the deceased died leaving an estate of a total
    and the amount = the total / 4.

% What the spouse does not own goes to the descendants; under a usufruct
% they inherit the bare ownership of the whole.
the descendants of a deceased share an amount
    if the deceased died leaving an estate of a total
    and a person takes a quarter of the estate of the deceased
    and the amount = the total - the total / 4.

the descendants of a deceased share an amount
    if the deceased died leaving an estate of the amount
    and it is not the case that
        a person takes a quarter of the estate of the deceased.

% Articles 735 and 753: the deceased's part is split equally among the
% branches, and a represented person's part among their own branches.
a deceased passes on an amount in the estate of the deceased
    if the descendants of the deceased share the amount.

a person passes on an amount in the estate of a deceased
    if the person is a branch of a parent in the estate of the deceased
    and it is not the case that
        the person is an heir in person of the deceased
    and the parent passes on a portion in the estate of the deceased
    and N is the count of each child such that
        the child is a branch of the parent in the estate of the deceased
    and the amount = the portion / N.

a person inherits an amount from a deceased
    if the person is a branch of a parent in the estate of the deceased
    and the person is an heir in person of the deceased
    and the parent passes on a portion in the estate of the deceased
    and N is the count of each child such that
        the child is a branch of the parent in the estate of the deceased
    and the amount = the portion / N.

% Articles 754 and 755: those who died first, renounced or are unworthy are
% represented by their descendants.
a person is represented in the estate of a deceased
    if the person is a branch of a parent in the estate of the deceased
    and the person passes on an amount in the estate of the deceased.

% Every estate is divided in full: the shares add up to it.
the shares of the estate of a deceased add up to an amount
    if the deceased died leaving an estate of a total
    and a first amount is the sum of each portion such that
        a person inherits the portion from the deceased
    and a second amount is the sum of each portion such that
        a person receives the portion from the deceased as surviving spouse
    and the amount = the first amount + the second amount.

scenario Marie is:
    Marie died leaving an estate of 240000.
    Paul is the spouse of Marie.
    Paul chose the usufruct.
    Anne is a child of Marie.
    Anne is a child of Paul.
    Bruno is a child of Marie.
    Bruno is a child of Paul.
    Bruno died before Marie.
    Chloe is a child of Bruno.
    David is a child of Bruno.
    Claire is a child of Marie.
    Claire is a child of Paul.
    Claire was convicted of killing Marie.
    Emma is a child of Claire.
    Denis is a child of Marie.
    Denis is a child of Paul.
    Denis renounced the estate of Marie.
    Fabien is a child of Marie.
    Fabien is a child of Paul.
    Fabien died before Marie.
    heirs expects answers ["Anne inherits 80000 from Marie", "Chloe inherits 40000 from Marie",
        "David inherits 40000 from Marie", "Emma inherits 80000 from Marie"].
    spouse expects answers [].
    usufruct expects answers ["Paul has the usufruct of the estate of Marie"].
    represented expects answers ["Bruno is represented in the estate of Marie",
        "Claire is represented in the estate of Marie"].
    unworthy expects answers ["Claire is unworthy to inherit from Marie"].
    totals expects answers ["the shares of the estate of Marie add up to 240000"].

scenario Jan is:
    Jan died leaving an estate of 90000.
    Lea is the spouse of Jan.
    Lea chose the usufruct.
    Kim is a child of Jan.
    Kim is a child of Lea.
    Tom is a child of Jan.
    Tom died before Jan.
    Uma is a child of Tom.
    Vic is a child of Tom.
    Vic died before Jan.
    Wim is a child of Vic.
    heirs expects answers ["Kim inherits 33750 from Jan", "Uma inherits 16875 from Jan",
        "Wim inherits 16875 from Jan"].
    spouse expects answers ["Lea receives 22500 from Jan as surviving spouse"].
    usufruct expects answers [].
    represented expects answers ["Tom is represented in the estate of Jan",
        "Vic is represented in the estate of Jan"].
    unworthy expects answers [].
    totals expects answers ["the shares of the estate of Jan add up to 90000"].

query heirs is:
    which person inherits which amount from which deceased.

query spouse is:
    which person receives which amount from which deceased as surviving spouse.

query usufruct is:
    which person has the usufruct of the estate of which deceased.

query represented is:
    which person is represented in the estate of which deceased.

query unworthy is:
    which person is unworthy to inherit from which deceased.

query totals is:
    the shares of the estate of which deceased add up to which amount.
